CONCLUSIONS: We demonstrated that lesion location and burden may contribute to depression comorbidity in MS. MS lesions disproportionately impacted fascicles in the depression network. MS1Depression patients had more disease than MS2Depression patients, which was driven by disease within the depression network. Future studies relating lesion location to personalized depression interventions are warranted.},
